Subject: Allow a build to use OpenSSL's own getaddrinfo fallback

What fails: the AROS headers define AI_PASSIVE and struct addrinfo, so
crypto/bio/bio_local.h and bio_addr.c select the getaddrinfo() path, and
the link fails with getaddrinfo, getnameinfo, freeaddrinfo and
gai_strerror undefined.

Why: on AROS these functions exist but are not plain C symbols. AROSTCP
provides them in miami.library (ABIv11 SDK clib/miami_protos.h, LVO
40-45) and, on mainline, also as Roadshow-style calls in bsdsocket.library;
they are reached through a library base (MiamiBase) with the macros from
<proto/miami.h>, which OpenSSL does not include or open. This build does
not integrate that interface. The API is not missing.

Fix: a build-defined macro, AROS_ST_NO_GETADDRINFO, undefines AI_PASSIVE
in bio_local.h, which OpenSSL already uses as its switch to its own
fallback (gethostbyname-based, IPv4 only). Only the aros-syncthing
Configure target defines the macro; other AROS builds are unaffected.

Scope: aros-syncthing's OpenSSL build only. aros-syncthing connects to a
numeric address on a socket it opens itself and does not resolve names
through OpenSSL, so the fallback is linked but not used.

Verification: link of a TLS client probe for ABIv11 has no undefined
symbols with this patch and four without it.

Status: local limitation of this build, not an upstream candidate. A
proper AROS integration would map these calls to MiamiBase and would need
runtime tests of the resolver, including IPv6.
---
--- a/crypto/bio/bio_local.h
+++ b/crypto/bio/bio_local.h
@@ -34,6 +34,16 @@
 #error openssl/bio.h included before bio_local.h
 #endif
 
+/*
+ * AROS_ST_NO_GETADDRINFO: the C library declares struct addrinfo and
+ * AI_PASSIVE, but getaddrinfo() and friends are not plain C functions
+ * there (on AROS they are calls through a library base, MiamiBase), so
+ * the build cannot link them. Use OpenSSL's own fallback instead.
+ */
+#ifdef AROS_ST_NO_GETADDRINFO
+#undef AI_PASSIVE
+#endif
+
 #ifdef AI_PASSIVE
 
 /*
